  "question": {
    "text": "The blocks <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;shown in the figure have masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>. the system is released from rest. The speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;has travelled a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> along the incline is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> &nbsp;<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0026_41c184911837.jpg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 250px;\" />"
  },
