  "solution": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;moves down the incline by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;shall move up by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. If the speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;then the speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></math>.<br /><br />From the conservation of energy: Gain in K.E. = loss in P.E.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>A</mtext></msub><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>B</mtext></msub><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>A</mtext></msub><mtext>g</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>B</mtext></msub><mtext>g</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br />Solving we get,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mtext>g</mtext><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>"
  }
